-- title:
--   Two β-substitutions generate the roof field at Nℓℓ'
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N,\ell,\ell',M$ be nonzero natural numbers with $\ell$ and $\ell'$ prime, $\ell \neq \ell'$, and $M = N\ell\ell'$. Assume `FunctionFieldGeneration M`, i.e. for every divisor $d$ of $M$ the series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,d\;(\mathrm{jq})$ — the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ applied to `jq`, given by shifting the Hahn-series support by multiplication by $d$ — lies in the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by $\mathrm{jq}$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,M\;(\mathrm{jq})$; assume also given modular-polynomial packets at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$, each consisting of a monic $\Phi \in (\mathbb{Z}[x])[y]$ of degree $\psi$ of the level (the sum of $N/d$ over squarefree divisors $d$) satisfying $\Phi(\mathrm{jq},\ \mathrm{jq}_{N}) = 0$. Write $F_{K}$ for the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by `divisorExpansions K` and $LF_{K}$ for its base change, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_{K}$. The conclusion is that the $L$-subalgebra of $LF_{M}$ generated by the union of the ranges of the two substitution maps $LF_{N\ell'} \to LF_{M}$ ($q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ followed by the inclusion coming from $N\ell'\ell \mid M$) and $LF_{N\ell} \to LF_{M}$ ($q \mapsto q^{\ell'}$ followed by the inclusion coming from $N\ell\ell' \mid M$) is the whole of $LF_{M}$.
--
--   This is the generation step for the roof of the degeneracy square at level $M = N\ell\ell'$: the base-changed modular function field at level $M$ is generated over $L$ by the images of the two $q$-power substitutions from the two intermediate levels. It is the input to the $(\beta,\beta)$-exchange identity [`ModularCurve.heckeBetaExchangeAt_of_primes_of_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeBetaExchangeAt_of_primes_of_ne).
-- source:
